RIP (Routing Information Protocol):- is a dynamic routing protocol used in networks to allow routers to exchange information about routes. RIP uses a distance-vector algorithm, where routers periodically broadcast their routing tables to neighboring routers. This helps in updating routing tables and maintaining accurate routes throughout the network.

-Certainly! Let's consider a network setup involving three routers (Router A, Router B, and Router C) with the following connections:

•Router A is connected to Router B.
•Router B is connected to both Router A and C. 
•Router C is connected to Router B.


-Scenario
Router A: Connected to Network A (192.168.10.0)
Router B: Connected to Network B (192.168.20.0)
Router C: Connected to Network C (192.168.30.0)

-The routers are connected as follows:

Router A is directly connected to Router B with IP addresses 10.0.0.1 and 10.0.0.2
Router B is directly connected to Router C with IP addresses 20.0.0.1 and 20.0.0.2

-Configuration Steps
For router A:-
>en
hashtag#conf t
hashtag#int gig0/0/0
hashtag#ip add 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0 
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#int se 0/1/0
hashtag#ip add 10.0.0.1 255.0.0.0
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#router rip
hashtag#network 192.168.10.0
hashtag#network 10.0.0.0
hashtag#version 2
hashtag#no auto summary 
hashtag#ex

For router B:-
>en
hashtag#conf t
hashtag#int gig0/0/0
hashtag#ip add 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0 
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#int se 0/1/0
hashtag#ip add 10.0.0.2 255.0.0.0
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#int se 0/1/1
hashtag#ip add 20.0.0.1 255.0.0.0
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#router rip
hashtag#network 192.168.20.0
hashtag#network 10.0.0.0
hashtag#network 20.0.0.0
hashtag#version 2
hashtag#no auto summary 
hashtag#ex

For router C:-
>en
hashtag#conf t
hashtag#int gig0/0/0
hashtag#ip add 192.168.30.1 255.255.255.0 
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#int se 0/1/0
hashtag#ip add 20.0.0.2. 255.0.0.0
hashtag#no shut
hashtag#ex
hashtag#router rip
hashtag#network 192.168.30.0
hashtag#network 20.0.0.0
hashtag#version 2
hashtag#no auto summary 
hashtag#ex
